(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Postoperative pain hyperalgesia and central sensitization contribute to both) Tj
T*
(acute severe pain and long-term chronic pain sequelae. Novel analgesic strategies) Tj
T*
(targeting pain pathophysiology are needed. This protocol describes a randomized) Tj
T*
(investigation of perioperative sub-dissociative esketamine combined with patient-) Tj
T*
(controlled analgesia. Methods: Patients with ectopic pregnancy requiring urgent) Tj
T*
(laparoscopic salpingectomy \(target n=84\) will be randomized 1:1 to receive intravenous) Tj
T*
(esketamine bolus \(0.25 mg/kg\) intraoperatively plus postoperative patient-controlled) Tj
T*
(esketamine-sufentanil analgesia versus enhanced opioid analgesia \(higher sufentanil dose) Tj
T*
(with saline placebo\). Primary outcome: pain sensitivity assessed via standardized) Tj
T*
(questionnaire on postoperative days 1, 2, and 7. Secondary outcomes: pain intensity) Tj
T*
(ratings, depressive symptom screening, serum inflammatory biomarkers \(BDNF,) Tj
T*
(prostaglandins\), adverse events. Sample size calculated for 80% power to detect a 1.2-unit) Tj
T*
(difference in primary pain sensitivity measure. Blinding, randomization, and allocation) Tj
T*
(concealment will ensure methodologic rigor.) Tj
